**Report template (ready for copy-paste):**

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| **Title** | Credentialed CORS Misconfiguration Enables Cross-Origin Read+Write of Customer VoIP Data |
| **Severity** | HIGH |
| **Asset** | `voip-management.easybell.de/api` |
| **Affected routes** | `/api/account`, `/api/accounts`, `/api/subscriber`, `/api/subscribers`, `/api/number`, `/api/numbers`, `/api/session` (all 7 Spring-handled routes) |
| **Summary** | All 7 Spring-handled API routes behind `voip-management.easybell.de` return `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: <arbitrary attacker-controlled origin>` with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` on both preflight OPTIONS and actual requests. Preflight also echoes any requested method (`PUT`, `POST` verified) and `authorization,content-type` headers. This allows any malicious website to make credentialed cross-origin requests on behalf of an authenticated user's browser, reading and writing customer VoIP account/number/subscriber configuration data without the user's knowledge. |
| **PoC** | See OPTIONS capture below |
| **Impact** | An attacker-controlled page can: (1) **read** full VoIP account/number/subscriber data via GET with `credentials:'include'`, (2) **modify** VoIP configuration via PUT/POST with `credentials:'include'` — all without any user interaction beyond visiting the attacker page while holding cached Basic auth or a voipSession token. |
| **Remediation** | Set `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` to a strict allowlist (e.g., only `https://my.easybell.com`), and remove `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` unless credentialed cross-origin access is explicitly required. |

**Evidence — OPTIONS preflight capture (2026-09-09 04:53:30 UTC):**

```
OPTIONS /api/account HTTP/1.1
Host: voip-management.easybell.de
Origin: https://evil.example.at
Access-Control-Request-Method: PUT
Access-Control-Request-Headers: authorization,content-type

HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://evil.example.at
Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true
Access-Control-Allow-Methods: PUT
Access-Control-Allow-Headers: authorization,content-type
```

