[NEXT] HUMAN: File voip-cors-cred-read-write at bugs.olivermaicher.eu NOW with this ready-to-submit body:
- Title: "CORS Misconfiguration Allows Credentialed Cross-Origin Read+Write of Customer VoIP Configuration (Reflection of Arbitrary Origin with Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true)"
- Asset: voip-management.easybell.de/api/{account,accounts,subscriber,subscribers,number,numbers,session} (nginx → Spring /api/v2/ rewrite; Sipwise NGCP backend)
- Severity: HIGH (CVSS ~8.6: AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N)
- Summary: 7 Spring-handled routes reflect any Origin verbatim in ACAO together with ACAC:true and echo requested methods (incl. PUT/POST) + authorization/content-type headers. Any hostile web page visited by a logged-in portal user can issue credentialed cross-origin fetch() against the customer VoIP API and read/write accounts/numbers/subscribers.
- Auth scheme: HTTP Basic realm `sipwisebroker` + Bearer `voipSession` (stored/cached in browser for the origin).
- Reproduction (per capture): `OPTIONS /api/account` with `Origin: https://evil.example.at`, `Access-Control-Request-Method: PUT`, `Access-Control-Request-Headers: authorization,content-type` → 200 with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://evil.example.at`, `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`, `Allow-Methods: PUT`, `Allow-Headers: authorization,content-type`.
- Evidence: 6 independent captures spanning 09-04 12:29, 09-05 13:12, 09-08 22:16, 09-09 04:53, 09-10 05:12, 09-10 09:48 UTC; identical response set; persistent >6 days; portal+API share ingress 62.27.117.123 but differ by host header → cross-origin from browser SOP perspective.
- Impact: cross-origin read/write → SIP credentials, subscriber/routing config disclosure and modification for any active portal session; no victim interaction beyond visiting attacker page.
- Remediation: replace origin reflection with strict allowlist; never pair ACAO-with-reflection and ACAC:true; set `Vary: Origin`; scope Allow-Methods/Allow-Headers to required values.

